Potential of air pollution increases when the ventilation coefficient is
(A) > 11000\ \text{m}^2/\text{s}
(B) > 7000\ \text{m}^2/\text{s}
(C) < 3600\ \text{m}^2/\text{s}
(D) < 6000\ \text{m}^2/\text{s}

[Diagram] A block of mass m_1 on a smooth inclined plane (angle \alpha) is connected to a hanging mass m_2. If m_2 goes down, the tension T in the string is
(A) \frac{m_1 m_2 g(1+\sin\alpha)}{m_2 - m_1}
(B) \frac{m_1 m_2 g(1-\sin\alpha)}{m_2 - m_1}
(C) \frac{m_1 m_2 g(1+\sin\alpha)}{m_1 + m_2}
(D) \frac{m_1 m_2 g(1-\sin\alpha)}{m_1 + m_2}

[Diagram] Power is transmitted from one shaft to a parallel shaft by external spur gears. If I_1 and I_2 are mass moments of inertia of gear‑1 and gear‑2 about their axes, the equivalent moment of inertia referred to the axis of gear‑1 is (where n = \omega_2/\omega_1)
(A) I_1 + I_2 n
(B) I_1 + I_2 n^2
(C) I_1 + \frac{I_2}{n}
(D) I_1 + \frac{I_2}{n^2}

[Diagram] A stone is projected from the base of an inclined plane (inclination \beta). If \alpha is the angle of projection with the horizontal, then for maximum range R on the inclined plane, the relationship is
(A) \alpha = 45^\circ - \frac{\beta}{2}
(B) \alpha = 45^\circ + \frac{\beta}{2}
(C) \alpha = \frac{45^\circ + \beta}{2}
(D) \alpha = 30^\circ + \frac{\beta}{2}

[Diagram] A chord is wrapped around a cylinder of radius r and mass m. If released from rest, the velocity of the centre after moving a vertical distance h is
(A) \sqrt{2gh}
(B) \sqrt{4gh/3}
(C) \sqrt{gh}
(D) \sqrt{gh/3}

[Diagram] A uniform rigid rod of length L and weight W is hinged to a wall at one end and supported horizontally by a vertical force F at the free end. If F is removed suddenly, the instantaneous vertical reaction at the hinged end is
(A) zero
(B) \frac{W}{4}
(C) \frac{W}{2}
(D) W

A solid circular rod of diameter d and length L is fixed at both ends. A torque T is applied at a distance L/4 from the left end. The maximum shear stress developed is
(A) \frac{16T}{\pi d^3}
(B) \frac{12T}{\pi d^3}
(C) \frac{8T}{\pi d^3}
(D) \frac{4T}{\pi d^3}

A shaft subjected to torsion experiences pure shear stress \tau at a point on the surface. The maximum principal stress at that point is
(A) \frac{\tau}{\sqrt{2}}
(B) -\sqrt{2}\,\tau
(C) \frac{\tau}{2}
(D) \tau

[Diagram] A beam is made of two identical bars AB and BC hinged at B. End A is fixed, end C simply supported. With load P as shown, the bending moment at end A is
(A) \frac{PL}{2}
(B) \frac{PL}{3}
(C) zero
(D) indeterminate

[Diagram] A rigid horizontal thin strip of length 2L is fixed at the free end of a circular cantilever (radius R, length L). Vertical forces P are applied at the strip ends. The vertical deflection at point A due to the load is (E and G are moduli)
(A) \frac{PL^3}{\pi R^4 G}
(B) \frac{PL^3}{\pi R^4 E}
(C) \frac{2PL^3}{\pi R^4 E}
(D) \frac{4PL^3}{\pi R^4 G}

[Diagram] With reference to the same cantilever beam but loaded differently, \frac{\delta_2}{\delta_1} =
(A) \frac{2}{3}
(B) \frac{21}{32}
(C) \frac{13}{12}
(D) \frac{5}{12}
